  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Counterproliferation Program (ICP): WMD Investigation and Operations (WIO) Course</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The WIO Course was delivered to 20 participants including crime scene investigators, state prosecutors, state security personnel, border patrol, financial analysts, and CBRN investigative managers across multiple ministries and agencies, to include the Ministry of Internal Affairs, Ministry of Defense, Ministry of Finance, Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the State Prosecutors Office, and the State Security Service of Georgia. The instruction provided the participants with highly specialized training on CBRN crime scene management and evidence handling techniques. The MIA Academy also received a donated equipment package designed to enhance the academys effort to develop an internal CBRN training curriculum. The curriculum will enable the MIA to generate personnel specialized in CBRN investigation operations and reduce their reliance on outside support.</narrative>
  </description>
